{
  "dom_id": "step-q2368",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Cars are entering a traffic jam at a rate of $7t$ cars per minute. If at time $t=0$ there are $60$ cars in the traffic jam, write an expression for $A(t),$ the total number of cars caught up in the traffic jam at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time measured in minutes.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(t)=7t$ be the rate at which the cars enter the traffic jam, and let $A(T)$ be the total number of cars in the traffic jam after $T$ minutes.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nA(T)=A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(T) & =A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60+{\\int }_{0}^{T}7t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={60+(\\frac{7{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =60+\\frac{7{T}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nA(t)=60+\\frac{7{t}^{2}}{2}.\n$$",
